[{:adr/consequences "{:canonical_home \"network-isekai is now explicit as the primary repo for this\\n                    session's game-engine-adjacent work; future network-isekai-\\n                    genre games land at public/games/gftd/{name}/ directly, not\\n                    as new standalone repos\", :manifest \"gftdcojp/isekai-network's repos.edn/west.yml entries (added at its\\n             creation, ADR-2607023200) removed in this same landing\", :issue_49_still_open \"the actual fix (PR#72) is unmerged -- this ADR documents\\n                         the investigation and consolidation decision, not a\\n                         claim that issue #49 is closed\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["gftdcojp/network-isekai (isekai.network) is the primary/canonical repo for\n    network-isekai-genre games; gftdcojp/isekai-network is archived and\n    superseded, content moved to network-isekai's public/games/gftd/shiro-pico/" "network-isekai issue #49 (kototama's Rust compile_game orphaned by the\n    clj-wgsl migration, no CLJS replacement) has a candidate fix in PR #72\n    (kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-engine-clj's .cljc compiler, verified\n    compiling+running production's real tanememi/logic.cljc in headless\n    Chromium) -- NOT merged, needs human review, touches the live boot path" "a reported string-decode bug in PR #72's test writeup could not be\n    reproduced via focused re-investigation (raw WebAssembly.instantiate\n    against the exact same compiled bytes decoded correctly in every case\n    tried) -- left open on the PR itself, not confirmed either way"], :adr/supersedes ["adr-2607023200-isekai-network-standalone-repo"], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "network-isekai-consolidation", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607023200-isekai-network-standalone-repo.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607032100-consolidate-engine-into-kami-engine-clj.edn" "gftdcojp/network-isekai issue #49, PR #72, PR #76" "gftdcojp/isekai-network (archived)"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607032400-network-isekai-primary-consolidation", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-03", :adr/body "# ADR 2607032400: network-isekai is the primary/canonical repo; isekai-network consolidated into it\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nEarlier this session, `gftdcojp/isekai-network` was created as a standalone repo\nfor \"Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico\" (ADR-2607023200), following the precedent set by\n`ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`'s own standalone-repo split (ADR-2607011816).\n\nInvestigation triggered by a naming-convention question (\"kotoba-lang/wgsl 実在\nしないの?\") led to discovering `gftdcojp/network-isekai` — a pre-existing, already\nlive-deployed project at `isekai.network` with almost exactly this session's\ntarget architecture: browser-based live CLJ game editing (edit `logic.cljc` →\ncompile → `WebAssembly.instantiate` → render via `kotoba-lang/webgpu`, zero Rust\nat runtime). Its compiler path broke when `kototama`'s Rust wrapper\n(`compile_game`/`compile_clj`) was removed with no CLJS replacement during the\nclj-wgsl migration (tracked as `network-isekai` issue #49). This session's\n`kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-engine-clj` (formerly `kotoba-lang/engine`,\nconsolidated per ADR-2607032100) is `.cljc` and targets the exact same\n`kami:engine/*@1.0.0` host-import ABI `kami.host` (in `kotoba-lang/webgpu`)\nalready implements — a strong, later-confirmed candidate to fix issue #49.\n\nThe user clarified explicitly: `network-isekai` (matching the live domain\n`isekai.network`) is the **primary/canonical** repo, not `isekai-network`. The\ntwo should be integrated, with `isekai-network`'s content moving into\n`network-isekai`, not the reverse.\n\n## Decision\n\n### `isekai-network` consolidated into `network-isekai`\n\n`gftdcojp/isekai-network`'s content (5-concept design bible +\n`games/01-netsurvivors/{logic.clj,scene.edn}`, the only concept with real code)\nmoved to `network-isekai`'s `public/games/gftd/shiro-pico/`, matching that\nrepo's own existing per-game convention (`public/games/gftd/{name}/{game.edn,\nlogic.cljc,scene.edn}` — see `tanememi`/`royale` as precedent). `logic.clj` was\nrenamed to `logic.cljc` (content unchanged — the kami-clj compiler subset needs\nno reader-conditional gating). `author.clj`/`deps.edn`/`.gitignore`/CI from the\nold standalone repo were NOT carried over — those were specific to\n`isekai-network`'s own repo-level tooling (the datalevin-authoring step);\n`scene.edn` is already the generated artifact and needs no re-authoring step\ninside `network-isekai`. Full accounting in\n`public/games/gftd/shiro-pico/PROVENANCE.md` (network-isekai).\n\nLanded via `network-isekai` PR #76 (additive only, new directory, no existing\nfile touched, no deploy/build config touched) — merged directly given the\nlow-risk additive nature, following this session's established\narchive-and-redirect pattern.\n\n`gftdcojp/isekai-network` is archived (not deleted) with its README pointing to\nthe new location — same non-destructive pattern as `kotoba-lang/engine`'s\narchival (ADR-2607032100).\n\n### Compiler-connection work (issue #49) — separate PR, not merged here\n\nA companion PR (`network-isekai` #72, `feat/issue-49-cljs-compiler`) wires\n`kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-engine-clj`'s CLJS compile path into\n`network-isekai`'s `boot!` as a fallback when the frozen pre-#14 Rust-built\n`window.kototama` artifact isn't loaded — verified compiling and running for\nreal in headless Chromium (production's actual `tanememi/logic.cljc`, 60 real\nticks, live entities). This PR is **not merged** — it touches the live game\nboot path and needs human review, unlike this ADR's additive game-directory\nmove. A reported string-decode discrepancy in that PR's own test writeup could\nnot be reproduced in a focused re-investigation (raw Node.js `WebAssembly.\ninstantiate` against the exact same compiled bytes, single- and multi-string-\nliteral cases, the exact `init` nested-call shape from `tanememi/logic.cljc`,\nand the CLJS-EDN-reader wrapping workaround all decoded correctly, byte-for-\nbyte and string-for-string) — most likely a test-harness artifact in that PR's\nspecific headless-Chromium setup rather than a defect in the compiler or\n`kami.host.cljs`, but this is not fully confirmed since the actual\nshadow-cljs/browser build wasn't re-run in this pass (no shadow-cljs toolchain\navailable in this session's environment without a slow fresh install). Left as\nan open follow-up on PR #72 itself, not blocking this ADR's game-move.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `network-isekai`/`isekai.network` is now explicitly the primary repo for this\n  session's game-engine-adjacent work; future network-isekai-genre games should\n  land there directly (`public/games/gftd/{name}/`), not as new standalone repos.\n- `gftdcojp/isekai-network`'s manifest registration (`repos.edn`/`west.yml`,\n  added when it was created) is removed in this same landing — see\n  `manifest-registration` below.\n- `kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems` and `kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs`\n  (both reference `isekai-network` as their example/reference game) got a short\n  pointer note added to their READMEs rather than a full rewrite of every\n  historical mention — those repos' own test artifacts (e.g.\n  `tests/fixtures/isekai-network-01-netsurvivors.wasm` filenames) are historical\n  record of what was actually tested and are left as-is.\n- The compiler-connection fix for `network-isekai` issue #49 remains open\n  (PR #72, pending review) — independent of this ADR's game-directory move,\n  which does not depend on issue #49 landing.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Keep `isekai-network` as a separate repo, cross-link only**: rejected per\n   explicit user direction — `network-isekai` is the primary repo, duplicated\n   parallel repos for the same underlying \"network-isekai game\" concept is\n   exactly the confusion this ADR resolves.\n2. **Rewrite every historical reference to `isekai-network` across all\n   dependent repos and this session's own ADRs**: rejected — ADRs are\n   point-in-time historical records (this session's own established\n   convention, e.g. ADR-2607011816/2607012000's supersession handling);\n   dependent-repo READMEs get a forward-pointing note, not a full rewrite.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607023200 (isekai-network standalone repo — now superseded by this ADR)\n- ADR-2607032100 (kotoba-lang/engine → kami-engine/kami-engine-clj consolidation\n  — the compiler piece this ADR's issue #49 connection depends on)\n- `network-isekai` issue #49, PR #72 (compiler connection, not merged), PR #76\n  (game-directory move, merged)\n- `gftdcojp/isekai-network` (archived)", :adr/decision "{:consolidation {:from \"gftdcojp/isekai-network@e904b7e84270e475c3c65700b8bd90068af854d0\", :to \"gftdcojp/network-isekai public/games/gftd/shiro-pico/\", :method \"plain copy (design/*.edn unchanged, games/01-netsurvivors/logic.clj\\n            renamed to logic.cljc content-unchanged, scene.edn unchanged) +\\n            new game.edn matching network-isekai's own manifest convention +\\n            PROVENANCE.md accounting for what was and wasn't carried over\", :not_carried_over \"author.clj/deps.edn/.gitignore/CI -- isekai-network's own\\n                       standalone-repo tooling (datalevin-authoring step),\\n                       unneeded now that scene.edn is already the generated\\n                       artifact living directly in network-isekai\", :pr \"network-isekai#76, merged directly (additive-only, low risk, matches\\n        this session's established archive-and-redirect landing pattern)\"}, :old_repo {:action \"archived (not deleted), README points to new location\", :repo \"gftdcojp/isekai-network\"}, :dependent_updates [\"kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems README -- short pointer note added\" \"kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs README -- short pointer note added\" \"historical test-artifact filenames (e.g. tests/fixtures/isekai-network-\\n    01-netsurvivors.wasm) left as-is -- record of what was actually tested\"], :compiler_connection_separate {:pr \"network-isekai#72 (feat/issue-49-cljs-compiler), NOT merged\", :why_separate \"touches the live game-boot path (kototama fallback logic in\\n                   isekai.game/boot!), unlike the purely-additive game-directory\\n                   move -- needs human review regardless of local verification\", :verification_done \"compiled + ran production's real tanememi/logic.cljc in\\n                        headless Chromium, 60 real ticks, live entities, wasm-\\n                        tools validate passed on the emitted bytes\", :open_item \"a reported entity-tag null-byte-prefix decode bug from that PR's\\n               test writeup could not be reproduced: raw Node.js\\n               WebAssembly.instantiate against byte-identical compiled output\\n               (single string, multi-string, the exact nested spawn-entity-\\n               inside-set-position! shape from tanememi/logic.cljc, and the\\n               CLJS-EDN-reader wrapping workaround PR#72 itself uses) all\\n               decoded correctly in every case tried. No shadow-cljs/real-\\n               browser re-run was done in this pass (toolchain not available\\n               without a slow fresh install) -- left open on PR#72, not\\n               resolved either way by this ADR\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user clarification 2026-07-03: network-isekai (isekai.network) is the\\n           PRIMARY repo, not isekai-network -- they should be integrated, with\\n           isekai-network's content moving into network-isekai\", :investigated [\"network-isekai is a pre-existing, live-deployed browser game-editing\\n    platform with almost exactly this session's target architecture -- edit\\n    logic.cljc -> compile -> WebAssembly.instantiate -> render via\\n    kotoba-lang/webgpu, zero Rust at runtime\" \"its compiler broke when kototama's Rust compile_game/compile_clj wrapper\\n    was removed with no CLJS replacement during the clj-wgsl migration,\\n    documented as an unresolved gap in kototama's own rust-migration.md and\\n    network-isekai issue #49\" \"kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-engine-clj (this session's compiler work) is\\n    .cljc and targets the exact kami:engine/*@1.0.0 ABI kami.host\\n    (kotoba-lang/webgpu) already implements -- verified by direct comparison\\n    of host-import->module-field strings against kami.host's aset calls\" \"network-isekai's existing per-game convention: public/games/gftd/{name}/\\n    {game.edn,logic.cljc,scene.edn} (tanememi/royale/etc. as precedent) --\\n    different shape than isekai-network's own author.clj+deps.edn+CI tooling,\\n    which was specific to being a standalone repo\"], :risk \"network-isekai is a live production site (isekai.network) -- the\\n         game-directory move (PR #76) is purely additive (new directory, no\\n         existing file touched) so was landed directly; the compiler-connection\\n         fix (PR #72) touches the live boot path and was explicitly left\\n         unmerged for human review regardless of how well local verification\\n         went\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"keep isekai-network as a separate repo, cross-link only\", :rejected_because \"explicit user direction: network-isekai is primary, a\\n                       duplicate parallel repo for the same game concept is\\n                       exactly the confusion this ADR resolves\"} {:option \"rewrite every historical isekai-network reference across all\\n            dependent repos and this session's own earlier ADRs\", :rejected_because \"ADRs are point-in-time historical records (established\\n                       convention this session, ADR-2607011816/2607012000's\\n                       own supersession handling); dependent READMEs get a\\n                       forward-pointing note instead of a full rewrite\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607032400: network-isekai is the primary/canonical repo; isekai-network consolidated into it", :adr/source-format "edn"}]